# Using ArchiPy Repositories

Each domain owns its data access under `repositories/{domain}/`.

Live: https://syntaxarc.github.io/ArchiPy/getting-started/project_structure/

## Layout

```text
repositories/{domain}/
├── adapters/                    # Domain wrappers around ArchiPy / external clients
│   └── {domain}_{purpose}_adapter.py
└── {domain}_repository.py       # Orchestrate adapters; map to repository DTOs
```

## Responsibilities

- `adapters/` — entity construction, query building, thin wrappers; prefer ArchiPy extras (`uv add "archipy[redis]"`) before inventing clients.
- `{domain}_repository.py` — orchestrates adapters, cache-aside patterns, maps results to repository DTOs (`*CommandDTO` / `*QueryDTO` / `*ResponseDTO`).
- Catch infrastructure exceptions at the adapter/repository boundary; re-raise as domain errors with `raise ... from e`.

## Domain Isolation

- Never import or call a repository from a different domain.
- Cross-domain reads go through the other domain’s **logic** class.

## Do Not

- Put business rules or `@postgres_sqlalchemy_atomic_decorator` here (that belongs in `logics/`).
- Create a top-level app `adapters/` package — domain adapters live under repositories.
- Leak raw driver exceptions into logics/services.
